Package: RegCompassR
Title: Multiome Regulatory Evidence and Metabolic Reaction Analysis
Version: 2.2.3
Authors@R: c(person(given = "RegCompass", family = "Developers", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "dev@example.com"))
Author: RegCompass Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: RegCompass Developers <dev@example.com>
Description: Integrates paired single-cell RNA and ATAC regulatory evidence
    with genome-scale metabolic reaction analysis. When two or more condition
    levels are available, RegCompass fits one condition-aware Pando design per
    broad cell type and uses condition-full outer-heldout TF-by-ATAC projections
    as the primary regulatory penalty. Jointly estimable edges form an auditable
    common-support component; edges non-estimable in one or both conditions
    contribute projectable structural zeros in those conditions. A supplied
    single-level condition directly uses original Pando infer_grn with unscaled
    predictors and no condition coefficients; an explicitly missing condition
    column is rejected. Condition-aware runs require the registered Pando 1.5.1
    C++ product and multitask kernels and stop immediately if native registration
    or execution is unavailable. Metacells retain the SuperCell2
    SCimplify_for_Seurat multimodal WNN and Walktrap workflow within each broad
    cell type. Conditions share that native graph, after which membership is
    split by condition and aggregated again through the native membership mode
    to guarantee pure metacells. Metacell RNA and ATAC counts use exact SuperCell
    membership. RNA latent expression uses normalized-unit empirical Bayes
    updates whose shrinkage weights are independent of library size; observed
    zeros retain continuous posterior evidence and are not threshold-clamped.
    Regulatory modifiers act on bounded RNA-support odds, GPR rules produce
    reaction expression, and each medium uses one shared union GEM and global
    FASTCORE completion. Directional structural vmax is solved once per shared
    model and target, then reused across metacells. Built-in medium scenarios are
    restricted to formulations with direct published-paper provenance. Depth
    matching, common-depth restriction, alpha sensitivity, zero-support
    sensitivity and link-saturation propagation are not part of the canonical
    workflow.
